	boss> sudo pkg install -y -r Emulab cracklib

Check serial number and iface of control nuc:
      sudo dmidecode -t system | grep Serial


Add profile to select image urn.

sort -r -n -t, -k 4 /tmp/mon.out | head -30

 B. Verify that N300 is properly connected with 10Gb interfaces.
    Swap in an experiment with the supermicro node and n300. Leigh has
    a profile for this. Or you can just swap in an experiment on the
    supermicro with the UHD tools.
    Login to the boss node and power on the n300 if it is off:
      wap power on n300-1
    Now login to ed1 and configure the 10Gb interfaces:
      sudo ifconfig eno7 inet 192.168.10.1 netmask 255.255.255.0 mtu 9000
      sudo ifconfig eno8 inet 192.168.20.1 netmask 255.255.255.0 mtu 9000
    Use ethtool to ensure there is a link on both. See if they ping.
    If neither pings, they might be backward. Try changing the IPs
    and try again. If they now ping, have Jon swap one end of the cables.

    Then enable one interface at a time and run uhd_usrp_probe or
    uhd_find_devices to make sure they can talk.




update interfaces set mac='3cecef43d353' where node_id='ed1' and iface'ipmi20';
update interfaces set mac='002590bc34a4' where node_id='ed1' and iface='eth2';
update interfaces set mac='002590bc36a8' where node_id='ed1' and iface='eth0';
update interfaces set mac='002590bc36a9' where node_id='ed1' and iface='eth1';
